drawing enemies  toward you hurting enemies is par for  the course in doom as it's often the  most viable tactic and it plays into the  game's cyclical murderous bliss  the tension of facing increasingly  durable enemies gives this system  longevity despite its repetitiveness to  keep up with the ever-growing board of  demons you must use resources earned for  your past feats to modify and upgrade  your weapons with new capabilities this  steadily feeds into your brash and  violent persona in order to maintain the  high of combat in the face of ever  growing tolerance for all things brutal  where a shotgun blast to the face was  once satisfying and effective enough you  ultimately desire the thrill and power  of an leashing a mortar like cluster  bomb from your double-barreled best  friend when he spent you'll be thankful  you upgraded your heavy assault rifle  with micro missiles that pierce the air  with a subtle whistle before lodging  under the skin of a demon and exploding  one after another secrets and hidden  areas aren't new to doom but the variety  of rewards you can reap are greater than  ever every bit of hardware including  weapons armor and their underlying  software can be augmented in multiple  ways the process of awkwardly  platforming your way across dooms Maps  in search of items does grow  increasingly tiresome as your pulse  drops to a murmur and your patience for  anything other than combat eventually  wears thin with a flush arsenal enhanced  physical abilities at the end of the  game you may opt to return to previous  missions to find items you may have  missed or to lay waste at higher  difficulty levels a multiplayer awaits  those who seek something new  unfortunately there's actually very  little knew about dooms multiplayer its  modes are few delivering the expected  assortment of match types including team  deathmatch and domination challenges and  it can be fun to step into the shoes of  a demon during a match but by and large  you won't find much in multiplayer that  hasn't been done before but what's there  is enjoyable in small doses thanks to  the fast pace of combat in the explosive  nature of dooms webinar more impressive  than multiplayer is snap map a mode that  allows you to create and share both  multi and single-player Maps online  tutorials walk you through the steps  involved in creating a map which is  already intuitive to begin with  snap map will live and die through the  creativeness of the community which has  already made a strong showing delivering  a collection of maps that range from  brutal to absurdly entertaining more  than multiplayer snap map is the cherry  on top of the new do  but without a doubt a loud and chaotic  campaign is due strongest component it's  straightforward and simple but it serves  its purpose to thrust you into  increasingly dire scenarios fueled by  rage and the spirit of heavy metal it  captures the essence of what made the  classic dune games touchstones of their  day and translates it to suit modern  palates with impressively rendered hell  escapes and a steady influx of  tantalizing upgrades doom is the product  of a tradition as oldest shooters and  while it's not the model to follow in  every case modern shooters could learn a  thing or two from dooms honed and  unadulterated
 

